		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=8659#p8659"><![CDATA[
Here is a few hours worth of work towards a conversion from Havok .hkx to COLLADA .dae Physics, using BulletColladaConverter.<br><br>Usage:<br>Start the demo Common/Api/Serialize/Simple Load/Binary to convert inputfile.hkx<br>Input has be to called inputfile.hkx, output will be havokToCollada<br>Drag the .dae file over ReleaseColladaDemo.exe to view results.<br><br>It has limited features, only converts sphere,box,convex, mopp shape, and a limited hinge constraint.<br><a href="http://www.bulletphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/index.php?dir=physics/demos/&amp;file=hkx2dae-0.01.zip" class="postlink">http://www.bulletphysics.com/ftp/pub/te ... e-0.01.zip</a> (8Mb zipfile)<br>The zipfile includes a converted version of the HavokMayaModules\2008\Tutorials\PhysicsBasics\tutorialEnd.mb<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=143" class="postimage" alt="havok_tutorial.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=144" class="postimage" alt="BulletCOLLADAViewer.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>Enjoy,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Thu Jun 05, 2008 3:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
